{#-
  In-brand 404 (roadmap Phase 9).

  Was the starter's plain markdown page with first-person copy ("let me know
  if you encounter more errors") -- wrong voice for a team, and it exposed the
  raw contact address to scrapers on the one page bots hit most.

  Uses the same near-black surface, mono status line and cyan accent as the
  rest of the site, and routes to the three places a lost visitor actually
  wants, rather than dead-ending on a link home.

  Note this page must use absolute paths that HtmlBasePlugin can rewrite: a
  404 is served from arbitrary URLs, so relative links would resolve against
  whatever path the visitor mistyped.
-#}

<div class="wrapper">
  <div class="cover" style="--cover-min-height: 70vh">
    <div class="error-page flow" data-centered>
      <p class="error-page__code">ERROR 404</p>
      <h1 class="font-display">Signal Lost</h1>
      <p class="hero-subline">
        That page doesn't exist, or it moved. The crow didn't see this one coming either.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-links cluster">
        <a class="button" data-button-variant="primary" href="/">Return to base</a>
        <a class="button" data-ghost-button href="/blog/">Read the blog</a>
        <a class="button" data-ghost-button href="/projects/">See the work</a>
      </div>

      <p class="error-page__note">
        If you followed a link here, tell us on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

